2|0@metalgearsolid^1438741537#ctrvj7l:Packersrule123$:Really? Wow, that's good to hear. Nice to know they aren't charging an arm and a leg for piles of crap.
2|0@metalgearsolid^1438742006#ctrvsur:MafiamanJ15$:Yeah, Western Arms GBB pistols are about the best of the best in terms of airsoft pistols that come out of Japan or anywhere else for that matter. The Heavyweight plastic gives it a really nice weight and feel to it and also gives it pretty good recoil, not to mention that since the slide is made of plastic, it has really good gas efficiency and the bb's fly as straight as an arrow with .28 gram bbs. Just because they're collector's items, doesn't mean that they can't perform. These Limited Edition WA pistols mostly get expensive since they are carefully handmade in a small workshop in Japan, (Shibuya Custom Works), and aren't exactly mass-produced. I paid about $450 for mine including the shipping cost to the US, and I have no regrets about it.
